# dvara-oss

HELP.md
target/
# The extraction's isolated Maven repository used to be written INSIDE this tree — 317 MB that
# `git add -A` would have swept into the initial commit. It now lives outside, and the
# emit verification fails if one appears here. This line is the third guard: even if both were
# undone, nothing can stage it.
.m2/
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
!**/src/main/**/target/
!**/src/test/**/target/

### STS ###
.apt_generated
.classpath
.factorypath
.project
.settings
.springBeans
.sts4-cache

### IntelliJ IDEA ###
.idea
*.iws
*.iml
*.ipr

### NetBeans ###
/nbproject/private/
/nbbuild/
/dist/
/nbdist/
/.nb-gradle/
build/
!**/src/main/**/build/
!**/src/test/**/build/

### VS Code ###
.vscode/

### macOS ###
.DS_Store

### Environment files (may contain API keys) ###
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

### ML model binaries — fetched at build time into target/, never committed ###
*.onnx

### Security-sensitive files ###
#
# Nothing below may be un-ignored. An exception for one file is really a grant of
# PERMISSION: with it in place, a key later dropped into a resources directory is
# staged by `git add -A` without a word. These rules are absolute so that cannot
# happen, and a key that genuinely needs to be in a build belongs outside the tree.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
credentials.json

### Local review scratchpad — seed data, review creds, docker harness (never commit) ###
/scratchpad/

### Node.js (local testing only) ###
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json

/scratch/
.claude/

# Local security-scan artifacts
.security-bin/
sbom.cdx.json


# JaCoCo coverage output (-Pcoverage)
**/target/site/jacoco/
**/target/site/jacoco-aggregate/
**/target/jacoco.exec

